\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces {\color  {blue}Nonlinear matter power spectra and matched BT/PL response ratios at representative redshifts. The upper panels show PL and BT spectra for the \(k_p=1\) and \(k_p=10\), \(m_s=1.5\) variants in the matched \(25\) and \(256\,h^{-1}\mathrm  {Mpc}\) boxes, together with the corresponding nonlinear theory curves for orientation. The lower panels show the direct simulation ratios BT/PL for each matched box and \(k_p\), plus the corresponding BT-theory/PL-theory ratios. In the fiducial $k_p=1$, $25\,h^{-1}\,\mathrm  {Mpc}$ box at $z=0$, BT/PL reaches $1.17$ at $k=20\,h\,\mathrm  {Mpc}^{-1}$ and $1.34$ at $k=40\,h\,\mathrm  {Mpc}^{-1}$. The spectra are measured on \(1024^3\) meshes. Vertical markers show the mesh Nyquist scales for the \(256\) and \(25\,h^{-1}\mathrm  {Mpc}\) boxes, and the gray high-\(k\) region marks scales beyond the \(25\,h^{-1}\mathrm  {Mpc}\) box Nyquist frequency \(k_{\rm  Ny}\simeq 129\,h\,\mathrm  {Mpc}^{-1}\). The shaded band around unity in the ratio panels marks a \(\pm 10\%\) reference interval; no halo-particle cut applies to this field-level statistic.}\relax }}{11}{figure.caption.28}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:power_spectra_ratio_z0}{{7}{11}{{\color {blue}Nonlinear matter power spectra and matched BT/PL response ratios at representative redshifts. The upper panels show PL and BT spectra for the \(k_p=1\) and \(k_p=10\), \(m_s=1.5\) variants in the matched \(25\) and \(256\,h^{-1}\mathrm {Mpc}\) boxes, together with the corresponding nonlinear theory curves for orientation. The lower panels show the direct simulation ratios BT/PL for each matched box and \(k_p\), plus the corresponding BT-theory/PL-theory ratios. In the fiducial $k_p=1$, $25\,h^{-1}\,\mathrm {Mpc}$ box at $z=0$, BT/PL reaches $1.17$ at $k=20\,h\,\mathrm {Mpc}^{-1}$ and $1.34$ at $k=40\,h\,\mathrm {Mpc}^{-1}$. The spectra are measured on \(1024^3\) meshes. Vertical markers show the mesh Nyquist scales for the \(256\) and \(25\,h^{-1}\mathrm {Mpc}\) boxes, and the gray high-\(k\) region marks scales beyond the \(25\,h^{-1}\mathrm {Mpc}\) box Nyquist frequency \(k_{\rm Ny}\simeq 129\,h\,\mathrm {Mpc}^{-1}\). The shaded band around unity in the ratio panels marks a \(\pm 10\%\) reference interval; no halo-particle cut applies to this field-level statistic.}\relax }{figure.caption.28}{}}
